    "chunk_text": "2. Description of the Land.\u2013 An allotment of Land depicted in below name and extent in the Preliminary Plan No. PP \u0db8\u0dc4 5639 dated 21.03.2006 prepared by the Surveyor General, situated in the village called Rambukpotha in the Udasiyapattuwa South Korale Minor Division in the Divisional Secretary\u2019s Division of Medadumbara in Kandy District of Central Province and bounded as:\n\nEOG 08-0169\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nO\u0d8b\u0d7d\u0d7e\u0d8b \u0d8e\u0d87\u0d7d\u0d7e\u0d8b S\u0d7e\u0d7c\u0d8d\u0d82\u0d88\u0d87 38 (a)\n\nOrder No. 74 of 2025\n\nMy Ref. No.: L03J/95/FR/184. Divisional Secretary\u2019s Ref. No.: KDS/MDB/4/2/1/64/10. BY virtue of the powers vested in me by the Order under Section 38(a) of Land Acquisition Act, (Chapter 460) I, Kuragamage Don Lal Kantha, Minister of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation, do hereby direct the Acquiring O\ufb03 cer or any other O\ufb03 cer authorized by him referred to Paragraph 1 of the Schedule to take possession of the Land speci\ufb01 ed in the corresponding entry in Paragraph 2 of that Schedule. K. D. L\u0d7a\u0d85 K\u0d7a\u0d87\u0d8d\u0d81\u0d7a, Minister of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation.\n\nMinistry of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation,\u201cMihikatha Medura\u201d, No. 1200/6, Rajamalwatta Road, Battaramulla,23rd July, 2025.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\n1. Acquiring O\ufb03 cer.\u2013 Divisional Secretary, Medadumbara.\n\n2. Description of the Land.\u2013 An allotment of Land depicted in below name and extent in the Final Preliminary Plan No. \u0db8\u0dc4 5609 dated 12.09.2004 prepared by the Surveyor General, situated in the village called Mangoda in the Udasiyapattuwa South Minor Division in the Divisional Secretary\u2019s Division of Medadumbara in Kandy District of Central Province and bounded as:\n\n01. Lot No. 2 \u2013 Golbokka Watta \u2013 Extent: 0.5526 Hectare North: Lot No. 1; East: TP 57452; South: TP 57452; West: TP 57452.\n\nEOG 08-0170\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
